Z||000017||grinthock||11-17-2001||07:49 AM||||The reason I am thinking O2....<P>With the scantool attached, the O2 is going EXTREME to EXTREME, .2 to .7 Volts, back and forth no matter WHAT the sitution is.<P>it matches the RPM movements.<P>No it's not throwing a code, checked, BUT if it's putting out erroneus readings the sensor is "working" according to our CRAP ECM which I am starting to realize we have.<P>Thanks for the help so far everyone, I will update you when I find out more.  <P>The good news is I found out at my new apartment I don't need to pass emissions!  So I am fine here that way, but I still need to get it fixed.<P>Back to the drawing board.||||reg||1
Z||000018||87GTZ34||11-17-2001||10:50 AM||||Back to your PCV...  Make sure the PCV valve is not bad a continuously sucking crank fumes into the intake.  Not a suspect but just an emlimination point.  Did you ever get to put a vac gauge on it?||||reg||1
Z||000019||grinthock||11-18-2001||01:06 AM||||I havn't had a chance to put a Vac guage on as of YET...  I am working on that, I am doing this before/after work, well before/after work the hardware place is closed.<P><BR>I think I may be getting somewhere, I pulled the MAP last night, I got one from a wrecker off another car but it doesn't FIT the electrical connector is diff, the fiero's there were stripped of MAP sensors.  Anyone know other cars that used it?  I pulled one from a Cav 2.8, it LOOKS identical but the electrical connector has different key'd slots.   So instead of changing it I used canned air to clean the intake hole, the vac tube, and the sensor itself, sprayed up into it, some black crap came out.<P>Put it back on, car SEEMS to be running FINE now, finally I think I have nailed it down, I will keep you all updated, saves me from buying a NEW Map if that was the problem.  I may replace it on spec when I get some extra cash just so I know it's reliable.  I will put my scantool back on when I get a chance and test it out see what values she's kickin.<P><BR>Have a great day and thanks for the help.||||reg||1
Z||000020||grinthock||11-24-2001||11:12 PM||||Work is killing me, here is some more questions I have hopefully someone can help me out<P>Fuel Pressure Reg.... It's on the same vac line as the MAP, I am thinking maybe either I have a vac leak on that line that is SLIGHT (How I find it I will NEVER KNOW!)  or my fuel pressure reg is bad and dumping fuel.  Map isn't the problem.<P><BR>How can I test the fuel pressure regulator?  Hell what does it look like and how do I replace it... Any and all help is appriciated!  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000021||87GTZ34||11-25-2001||12:39 PM||||Well since you asked...  They make a vacuum tester that allows you to (inverse) pump (I guess that's evacuate) whatever you want to test.  So you disconnect the line going to the regulator and connect it to the pump, put about 20 inches of vac on it and watch it for a few minutes.  It should drop ever so slightly if any to be acceptable.  I picked up a cheapy pump/tester from discount auto for about $40 USD.  From this I learned that my EGR switch was a vacuum (open) and also the manifold vacuum side of the evap canister so I bypassed both. GL||||reg||3
Z||000022||grinthock||11-26-2001||10:26 PM||||can I work on the FPR without removing the plenum?<P>Also if I wanted to replace the vac line going from the plenum to the FPR, how would I do it?  Where do I get it?  Do I have to order one from GM?||||reg||1
Z||000023||BC-GT||11-26-2001||10:45 PM||||Hey Grint, I'm in the same boat as you right now, tried plumbing a new PCV hose through the other day and accidently pulled that little bastard off myself. I don't think you can get it back without pulling the plenum myself, hell, I couldn't even see the nipple the hose goes on. On a brighter note, I searched all the newsgroups through Metacrawler(search engine) and I think you are definitely on the right track, saw hundreds of posts about the exact same problems and symptoms.<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
